<title>SPAIN: Spain details economic forecast through 2000.</title>
<headline>Spain details economic forecast through 2000.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>In its stability plan through the year 2000, Spain gave the following economic forecasts:</p>
<p> GDP, AGGREGATES(% real variation)   1997  1998  1999 2000  avg</p>
<p> Private consumption			2.7   2.7   2.8   3.0  2.8</p>
<p> Public consumption			-0.3   1.0   1.0   1.0  0.7</p>
<p> Gross capital formation		  4.0   7.1   7.8   5.6  6.1</p>
<p> National demand			    2.5   3.4   3.7   3.3  3.2</p>
<p> Exports of goods and services	  9.9   9.5   9.7   8.8  9.5</p>
<p> Imports of goods and services	  8.1   9.6  10.0   8.9  9.1</p>
<p>Foreign balance</p>
<p> (as percentage to GDP growth)	  0.4  -0.2  -0.3  -0.2 -0.1</p>
<p> Gross domestic product		   3.0   3.2   3.4   3.2  3.2</p>
<p> OTHER VARIABLES  Private Consumption deflator (%varia)</p>
<p>						  2.5   2.3   2.2   2.2  2.3</p>
<p> Employment (% variation)		 2.0   2.2   2.3   2.1  2.1</p>
<p>--Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2167</p>
</text>
